  "manual": "GLOSSARY. **Spell Counter** = a token most cards in this deck bank each time a Spell resolves; nearly every Endymion/Mythical Beast Pendulum gains 1 (Jackal King and Master Cerberus gain 2) whenever ANY Spell resolves — yours or the opponent's. Counters are the deck's currency: you spend them to Special Summon, negate, banish, and destroy. **Scale / Pendulum Zone** = the two side zones; put a Pendulum monster in each and you may once per turn Pendulum Summon monsters whose Level is strictly between the two scale numbers, from hand and from face-up Pendulum monsters in your Extra Deck. **Face-up in the Extra Deck** = when a Pendulum monster would leave the field it lands face-up in the Extra Deck, where Magister of Endymion and Jackal King can re-summon it.\n\n=== BIG PICTURE ===\nYou are a combo/control Spellcaster deck. You play a wall of cantrip Spells (3x Upstart Goblin, 3x Into the Void, Pot of Desires, the Spellbook mini-engine) whose ONLY real purpose is to make Spell Counters pile onto your Pendulum monsters and onto Magical Citadel / Mythical Institution. Once counters are stacked you convert them into a Special-Summon chain that ends on **Endymion, the Mighty Master of Magic** as an omni-negate boss, backed by **Mythical Beast Jackal King** (monster-effect negate) and **Master Cerberus** (effect-destruction-immune 2800 beater with a banish). Citadel and Institution redirect destruction to counter-removal, so the board is very hard to break by popping.\n\n=== THE ENGINE PIECES ===\n- **Spell Power Mastery (3, your best starter):** adds ANY 'Endymion' card from Deck (grab Endymion the boss, or a Servant/Magister, or Magical Citadel), and places Spell Counters equal to how many Spell Power Mastery you control/GY (ramps as you play more copies). This one card is your search + your first counters.\n- **Servant of Endymion (3):** in a Pendulum Zone it gains a counter per Spell; remove 3 counters to Special Summon ITSELF from the zone PLUS any 1000+ ATK counter-holder from Deck (fetch Master Cerberus / Jackal King / another Endymion). Its monster effect: once per opponent's turn discard 1 to place a counter on every card you control that can hold one — mass-loads counters before an Endymion wipe or to arm negates.\n- **Magister of Endymion (2):** remove 3 counters to SS itself from the zone + revive 1 face-up monster from your Extra Deck; and once per opponent's turn remove 3 counters to SS a counter-holder from Deck (on-turn disruption/extension).\n- **Reflection of Endymion (1):** remove 3 counters to SS itself + a monster from HAND; on Special Summon it bounces 1 opponent card AND 1 of your own counter-cards, re-banking the counters — a free interruption that recycles.\n- **Mythical Beast Jackal (2, Level 1):** Pendulum effect self-destructs to seed a counter; monster effect removes 3 counters + tributes itself to SS a 'Mythical Beast' from Deck (tutor Jackal King / Master Cerberus / Bashilisk / Garuda). Being Level 1 it feeds Linkuriboh, Relinquished Anima, and Artemis.\n- **Mythical Beast Master Cerberus (1, Level 8 / 2800):** Pendulum effect self-destructs to ADD a Lv7-or-lower Mythical Beast from Deck; monster effect is immune to effect destruction while 4+ counters sit on your field, and removes 4 counters to banish an opponent monster and steal its ATK.\n- **Mythical Beast Jackal King (3):** on-board negate — banks 2 counters per Spell and, once per turn, removes 2 counters to negate+destroy an opponent's monster effect. Its Pendulum effect self-destructs to revive a Mythical Beast Pendulum from the Extra Deck. Three copies = layered negates.\n- **Magical Abductor (1):** counter monster; remove 3 to add a Pendulum from Deck, or a Level-1 Spellcaster.\n- **Mythical Beast Bashilisk (1):** Pendulum effect recycles a Spellcaster Pendulum from ED into the Deck AND draws 1; monster effect bounces a Mythical Beast back to hand.\n- **Mythical Beast Garuda (1):** Pendulum effect destroys another S/T (and itself); monster effect is a soft handtrap — when the opponent summons, remove 3 counters to SS itself from hand and bounce their monster.\n- **Field/Continuous banks:** **Magical Citadel of Endymion (2)** stores counters, lets you pay counter-costs from it, and survives destruction by removing 1 counter. **Mythical Institution (3)** is a Level-based tutor (remove N counters -> add a counter-holder of Level N from Deck or face-up ED) that also tanks destruction. **Mythical Bestiary (1)** mills 2 and places up to 2 counters; if destroyed it Special Summons a counter-holder from Deck.\n- **Spellbook mini-engine:** Spellbook Magician of Prophecy searches Spellbook of Secrets -> Spellbook of Knowledge (dump a Spellcaster or Spellbook, draw 2). Extra Spell activations = extra counters, and it fuels **Crowley, the First Propheseer** in the Extra Deck.\n- **Magia Magic - Thunder of Judgment (1):** a Magistus/Endymion Spell — pay a Magistus or 2 counters to EITHER Special Summon a Spellcaster from hand/face-up ED/GY, OR banish 1 card on the field. Flexible extender + spot removal, and pairs with Artemis (Magistus) in the Extra Deck.\n\n=== A TYPICAL GOING-FIRST LINE ===\n1) Resolve Spell Power Mastery: search Endymion the boss (or a missing piece) and bank your first counters. 2) Chain cheap Spells (Upstart, Into the Void once you hold 3+, Pot of Desires, the Spellbooks) to flood counters onto a Servant/Magister set in a Pendulum Zone and onto Citadel/Institution. 3) Spend counters: Servant SS's itself + a Deck monster; Magister revives from the Extra Deck; Jackal tutors a Mythical Beast; you build to **Heavymetalfoes Electrumite** (2 Pendulum monsters -> add a Pendulum from Deck; pop your own card to SS a Lv4-or-lower Pendulum from Deck) and then **Selene, Queen of the Master Magicians** (banks counters on summon, then removes 3 to revive a Spellcaster — into **Accesscode Talker** if you want damage). 4) Set the endboard: put **Endymion** in a Pendulum Zone or the Monster Zone (his Pendulum effect removes 6 counters to SS himself and destroy up to as-many-cards-as-you-control-that-hold-counters). Leave counters banked so Endymion has one (targeting- and destruction-immune) and Jackal King(s) can negate. Optionally hold **I:P Masquerena** to make **S:P Little Knight** (banish disruption) on the opponent's turn.\n\nENDBOARD (ideal): Endymion (Quick-Effect omni-negate: bounce your own counter-card to negate+destroy anything, protected while he holds a counter) + 1-2 Jackal King (monster-effect negate, 2 counters each) + Master Cerberus (effect-destruction-immune 2800, banish) + Magical Citadel + Mythical Institution banking counters, with S:P Little Knight or Apollousa as extra interruption from I:P Masquerena.\n\n=== GOING SECOND ===\nYou are a strong turn-2 deck. **Triple Tactics Talent** (after the opponent uses a monster effect on your turn) draws 2, steals a monster, or peeks-and-shuffles. Dig with Pot of Desires / Upstart / Into the Void, load counters, then use **Endymion's Pendulum effect as a board wipe** (destroy up to N cards after stacking counter-holders), **Master Cerberus** and **Magia Magic** to banish, **Reflection / Garuda** to bounce, and **Underworld Goddess of the Closed World** (Link-5, uses an opponent's monster as material and negates on summon) or **Knightmare Unicorn** to punch through, finishing with **Accesscode Talker**.\n\n=== HANDTRAP NAVIGATION ===\n- **Called by the Grave (1)** answers Ash Blossom / Maxx \"C\" / Nibiru by banishing + negating the same-named effect.\n- **Ash Blossom** on Spell Power Mastery or a Spellbook: you have redundancy (3x Mastery + Institution + Abductor + Servant/Jackal tutors) — eat it and continue with a different starter.\n- **Maxx \"C\":** keep the line SHORT (Electrumite + one negate) or turn it around with Triple Tactics; don't over-extend into a free draw engine.\n- **Nibiru, the Primal Being:** count your Special Summons — Endymion floods fast. Stop at 4 summons if Nibiru is live, or bait it; Endymion / Master Cerberus is your post-Nibiru beater and can rebuild off banked counters and cards face-up in the Extra Deck.\n- **Droll & Lock Bird:** shuts the search engine — pivot to Pendulum Summoning the monsters already in hand and to Endymion's Pendulum wipe, which need no searching.\n\n=== WEAKNESSES ===\n- **Anti-Spell floodgates are lethal:** Anti-Spell Fragrance / Mystic Mine stop your Spells, which stops counters, which stops the entire engine. These are your worst matchup.\n- **Droll & Lock Bird** cripples the cantrip/search chain.\n- **Bounce/banish removal** (Evenly Matched, Lightning Storm, Forbidding, Kaijus) sidesteps Citadel/Institution, which only redirect DESTRUCTION.\n- **Bricking:** hands of only high-scale pendulums with no starter stall you — but 3x Spell Power Mastery, Magical Abductor, Mythical Institution, and the Servant/Jackal tutors keep the starter count high.\n- The board leans on counters; a first-Spell negate or a well-timed disruption before you bank counters slows the whole turn.",
  "main": [
